lesson: 168
title: The score that makes the average
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: An average of 80 over 4 tests means the 4 marks add up to 4 × 80 = 320.
explain: If the first three marks add up to 228, the fourth must be 320 − 228 = 92.
explain: If you know the average of the first three instead, their total is 3 times that average.
vars: a=name m=65..95 A=60..95 s1=55..100 s2=55..100
let: s3 = 3 * A - s1 - s2
let: x = 4 * m - 3 * A
need: s3 >= 50 && s3 <= 100
need: x >= 40 && x <= 100
answer: 4 * m - 3 * A
exercise: {a} scored {s1}, {s2} and {s3} in three tests. What must {a.he} score in the fourth test to have an average of {m}?
exercise: {a}'s average over three tests is {A}. What mark does {a.he} need in the fourth test for an average of {m} over all four?
exercise: In three games a team scored {s1}, {s2} and {s3} points. How many points must it score in the fourth game so that the average for the four games is {m}?
exercise: {a} read {s1} pages on Monday, {s2} on Tuesday and {s3} on Wednesday. How many pages must {a.he} read on Thursday to read {m} pages a day on average over the four days?
exercise: The average of three numbers is {A}. What fourth number makes the average of all four numbers {m}?
exercise: A shop sold {s1}, {s2} and {s3} loaves on three days. How many must it sell on the fourth day for an average of {m} loaves a day?
test: What must the fourth number be if the first three are {s3}, {s1} and {s2}, and the average of all four is {m}?
test: After three quizzes {a} has an average of {A} points. {a.He} wants to end the four quizzes with an average of exactly {m}. How many points does the last quiz have to bring?
test: A runner ran {s2}, {s3} and {s1} laps in three weeks. To average {m} laps a week over four weeks, how many laps must the runner run in the fourth week?
test: A class collected {s1} kg of paper in the first week, {s3} kg in the second and {s2} kg in the third. Its goal is {m} kg a week on average over four weeks. How many kg must it collect in the fourth week?
exercise: What score does {a} need on the fourth test to average {m}, if {a.his} first three scores were {s1}, {s2} and {s3}?
exercise: A basketball team in Chicago scored {s2}, {s1} and {s3} points in three games. How many points does it need in the fourth game for an average of {m} points per game?
exercise: {a} has averaged {A} points over three quizzes. How many points must {a.he} get on the fourth quiz so that the average of all four is {m}?
exercise: A bakery in Leeds sold {s1} pies on Monday, {s2} on Tuesday and {s3} on Wednesday. How many pies must it sell on Thursday to average {m} pies a day over the four days?
exercise: Three numbers have a mean of {A}. Which number must be added as the fourth so that the mean of all four is {m}?
exercise: {a} swam {s3}, {s1} and {s2} lengths on three days at a pool in Brisbane. How many lengths must {a.he} swim on the fourth day to average {m} lengths a day?
exercise: Over three weeks a class in Ottawa collected {s1}, {s2} and {s3} cans for a food drive. How many cans must it collect in week four so that the weekly average is {m}?
exercise: The mean of four numbers is {m}. Three of them are {s1}, {s2} and {s3}. What is the fourth number?
test: {a}'s marks so far are {s2}, {s3} and {s1}. To finish the term with an average of {m} over four marks, what must the next mark be?
test: A cricketer in Auckland made {s1}, {s3} and {s2} runs in three innings. How many runs must he make in the fourth innings to average {m} runs an innings?
test: If three tests averaged {A} and the average over four tests is to be {m}, what score is needed on the remaining test?
test: A farm stand in Maine sold {s3} baskets of berries on the first day, {s2} on the second and {s1} on the third. For the four days to average {m} baskets a day, how many baskets must be sold on day four?
test: Four numbers average {m}. The average of the first three is {A}. What is the last number?
test: {a} cycled {s1} km, {s2} km and {s3} km on three Saturdays in Scotland. How many km must {a.he} cycle on the fourth Saturday to average {m} km per Saturday?
exercise: got {s1}, {s2}, {s3} in 3 tests, need avg {m} over 4. what i gotta get on the 4th
exercise: me average over 3 tests is {A+1} — no wait, {A}. what i need on the 4th for {m} avg
exercise: Sam says {4*m} plus {3*A}, so {4*m+3*A}?? nah that's way off. 3 games {s1} {s2} {s3}, avg over 4 is {m}, what's game 4 score really
exercise: team scored {s1}, {s2}, {s3} in 3 games, coach is 6 foot tall lol, need average {m} for 4 games. how many points in game 4
test: avg after 3 tests is {A}, want {m} for all 4, wat mark i need in the last one
test: marks {s1} {s2} {s3}, wanna average {m} over four. 4th mark?
test: {a} scored {s1}, {s2+1} — no hang on, {s2} — and {s3} in three quizzes, wants average {m} over four. 4th quiz score?
exercise: {a} missed a week of school when {a.his} grandmother passed away. {a.His} average over three tests is {A}. What must {a.he} score in the fourth test to have an average of {m}?
exercise: report says {a} is "not working to {a.his} potential" — means slacking. scored {s1}, {s2}, {s3}. what's {a.he} gotta get on the 4th to average {m}, or mum'll kill {a.him}
test: {a} was economical with the truth and told Mum {a.his} average was far higher; really it is {A} after three tests. Which score in test four would make the real average {m}?
exam: It is given that {a} attained marks of {s1}, {s2} and {s3} in three examinations. Determine the mark that {a.he} must attain in a fourth examination in order that the mean of all four marks be {m}.
exam: Whereas the mean mark of {a} over three tests is {A}, ascertain the mark requisite in a fourth test for the mean over all four tests to equal {m}.
exam: Ascertain the fourth number, given that the arithmetic mean of three numbers is {A} and the arithmetic mean of those three numbers together with the fourth is {m}.
exam: A candidate's marks in three papers are {s1}, {s2} and {s3}. State the mark which the candidate must obtain in a fourth paper so as to attain an average of {m} across the four papers.
